window.docContents[21].resolve({"/rules/PL1006/#PL1006-fix":{"contents":"1. Remove an unnecessary unsafe marker.2. Replace partial def by a definition with structural recursion or a termination_by measure and decreasing_by proof.3. If the computation must stay unsafe or partial, move it to a separate, unclaimed dependency package; a claimed module cannot import an excluded module of its own package (PL2004). Where a claimed executable reaches it, it is reported as a trusted unsafe-computation or partial-computation boundary, which fails under checked execution (PL3002).\n\n","context":"Plumb for Lean rule reference\u0009Rule index\u0009PL1006: Unsafe and partial declarations require exact helper authentication","header":"How to fix it","id":"/rules/PL1006/#PL1006-fix"},"/rules/PL2005/#PL2005-fix":{"contents":"1. Remove uses of debug.skipKernelTC, addDecl with unchecked values, or other metaprograms that add unchecked declarations; state and prove the theorem normally.2. Do not edit sources while an audit runs; rerun it.3. For an editor pending result, run lake lint (or lake lint -- --fresh).\n\n","context":"Plumb for Lean rule reference\u0009Rule index\u0009PL2005: Required admission and source evidence must be complete","header":"How to fix it","id":"/rules/PL2005/#PL2005-fix"},"/rules/PL4003/#PL4003-fix":{"contents":"1. If the example is actually valid, remove the lean-fail marker so it is checked as positive.2. If it should fail, edit the example so it fails for the documented reason, and write a pattern that matches that one error message.3. Keep patterns to literal fragments joined by .* and alternatives separated by |.\n\n","context":"Plumb for Lean rule reference\u0009Rule index\u0009PL4003: Negative examples require completed intended rejection","header":"How to fix it","id":"/rules/PL4003/#PL4003-fix"},"/rules/PL5002/#PL5002-fix":{"contents":"1. Add /-- … -/ immediately before the declaration, stating purpose, domain and hypotheses, result and boundary (standard §5.1).2. Include a # Intent section with the requirement the claim must meet (standard §5.2); a missing Intent section is PL5003.\n\n","context":"Plumb for Lean rule reference\u0009Rule index\u0009PL5002: Registered public material declarations require docstrings","header":"How to fix it","id":"/rules/PL5002/#PL5002-fix"}});